# Dramatic Accusation on Bot2's Ornithopter: "When this Aura enters, tap enchanted creature" taps it on turn 3, and "Enchanted creature doesn't untap
# during its controller's untap step" (CR 502.3) keeps it tapped through Bot2's turn-4 untap step. {U}{U}: with one blue source left on turn 3
# (Mox Sapphire and Mox Ruby: two mana, one of them blue) the ability is refused; on turn 5 with both Sapphires untapped it is paid exactly ({U}{U}, the pool
# empty afterwards) and resolves: the Ornithopter is shuffled into Bot2's library (Bot2's library is shuffled once) and the Aura, its creature gone,
# goes to the graveyard (CR 704.5m).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Dramatic Accusation
Island
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter x4
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dramatic Accusation.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
! Bot1.Battlefield.Dramatic Accusation.Activate(Mana: short)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Dramatic Accusation.Activate
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
Bot2.Shuffles = 1
Bot1.Graveyard = Dramatic Accusation
